{"id":"G2031","lemma":"ἔπος","transliteration":"epos","sayIt":"epos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, neuter","gloss":"a word","meaning":"ἔπος, -εος (-ους), τό\n[in LXX: Zec.7:3, Sir.44:5 * ;]\na word: ὡς ἔ. εἰπεῖν (cl.), so to speak: Heb.7:9.†\nSYN.: λόγος, reasoned speech; ῥῆμα, mere articulated utterance; ἔ., the articulated expression of a thought (AS)","glosses":["speak"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"heb-7","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"to speak","kjv":"I may so say"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Hebrews 7:9","note":"We can say that through Abraham even Levi, who receives tithes, has paid tithes,","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20310","lemma":"ἐκλικμάω","transliteration":"eklikmaō","gloss":"to sift"},{"id":"G20311","lemma":"ἐκλογιστής","transliteration":"eklogistēs","gloss":"accountant"},{"id":"G20312","lemma":"ἐκλογιστία","transliteration":"eklogistia","gloss":"reckoning: accounts"},{"id":"G20313","lemma":"ἐκμελίζω","transliteration":"ekmelizō","gloss":"to dismember"},{"id":"G20314","lemma":"ἐκπαίζω","transliteration":"ekpaizō","gloss":"to mock"},{"id":"G20315","lemma":"ἐκπετάννυμι","transliteration":"ekpetannumi","gloss":"gaping"},{"id":"G20316","lemma":"ἐκπιάζω","transliteration":"ekpiazō","gloss":"to squeeze"},{"id":"G20317","lemma":"ἐκπολιτεύω","transliteration":"ekpoliteuō","gloss":"to corrupt"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}